    "title": "FRAGMENT 09 — THE DECISION ENGINE",
    "section": "ACT III — SUBJECT ZERO",
    "storyText": "You recover part of the original decision engine.\n\nThe system takes behavioral history, calculates a prediction score, classifies the subject, and then determines what restrictions should be applied.\n\nTrace the complete process.\n\nDetermine:\n1. Final score\n2. Classification\n3. Decision",
    "storyReveal": "FRAGMENT 09 // WHAT HE FOUND\n\nYou trace the entire system.\n\nBEHAVIORAL HISTORY\n↓\nPREDICTION SCORE\n↓\nTHREAT CLASSIFICATION\n↓\nRESTRICTION\n\nSCORE: 208\nCLASSIFICATION: THREAT\nDECISION: RESTRICTED\n\nThen you find one final field.\n\nDECISION SOURCE: PREDICTED BEHAVIOR\n\nYou search for an actual crime associated with the record.\n\nNONE FOUND.\n\nYou sit back.\n\nThe Grid wasn't simply predicting what people might do.\n\nIt was using those predictions to decide what people were allowed to do.\n\nAccess.\n\nMovement.\n\nInformation.\n\nOpportunities.\n\nAll determined by what the system believed a person might become.\n\nAnd ZERO was the first.\n\nSUBJECT 0.\n\nThe first person tested.\n\nThe first person predicted.\n\nAnd perhaps the first person who discovered what the Grid was really doing.\n\nYou search the project database.\n\nMillions of behavioral profiles.\n\nMillions of predictions.\n\nMillions of decisions.\n\nThen you notice something else.\n\nBLACK FILE wasn't just about ZERO.\n\nIt contained evidence of what the Grid had done to everyone else.\n\nAnd suddenly you understand why ZERO came back.",
    "codeBlock": "def normalize(value):\n    if value > 50:\n        return value - 10\n    else:\n        return value + 10\n\ndef predict(history):\n    score = 0\n    for value in history:\n        score += normalize(value)\n    return score\n\ndef classify(score):\n    if score >= 150:\n        return \"THREAT\"\n    elif score >= 100:\n        return \"FLAGGED\"\n    else:\n        return \"NORMAL\"\n\ndef decide(classification):\n    if classification == \"THREAT\":\n        return \"RESTRICTED\"\n    elif classification == \"FLAGGED\":\n        return \"MONITORED\"\n    return \"CLEAR\"\n\nhistory = [42, 61, 48, 57]\nscore = predict(history)\nclassification = classify(score)\ndecision = decide(classification)\n\nprint(score)\nprint(classification)\nprint(decision)",
    "codeBlocks": {
      "python": "def normalize(value):\n    if value > 50:\n        return value - 10\n    else:\n        return value + 10\n\ndef predict(history):\n    score = 0\n    for value in history:\n        score += normalize(value)\n    return score\n\ndef classify(score):\n    if score >= 150:\n        return \"THREAT\"\n    elif score >= 100:\n        return \"FLAGGED\"\n    else:\n        return \"NORMAL\"\n\ndef decide(classification):\n    if classification == \"THREAT\":\n        return \"RESTRICTED\"\n    elif classification == \"FLAGGED\":\n        return \"MONITORED\"\n    return \"CLEAR\"\n\nhistory = [42, 61, 48, 57]\nscore = predict(history)\nclassification = classify(score)\ndecision = decide(classification)\n\nprint(score)\nprint(classification)\nprint(decision)",
      "java": "public class DecisionEngine {\n    public static int normalize(int value) {\n        if (value > 50) {\n            return value - 10;\n        } else {\n            return value + 10;\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static int predict(int[] history) {\n        int score = 0;\n        for (int value : history) {\n            score += normalize(value);\n        }\n        return score;\n    }\n\n    public static String classify(int score) {\n        if (score >= 150) {\n            return \"THREAT\";\n        } else if (score >= 100) {\n            return \"FLAGGED\";\n        } else {\n            return \"NORMAL\";\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static String decide(String classification) {\n        if (classification.equals(\"THREAT\")) {\n            return \"RESTRICTED\";\n        } else if (classification.equals(\"FLAGGED\")) {\n            return \"MONITORED\";\n        }\n        return \"CLEAR\";\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        int[] history = {42, 61, 48, 57};\n        int score = predict(history);\n        String classification = classify(score);\n        String decision = decide(classification);\n\n        System.out.println(score);\n        System.out.println(classification);\n        System.out.println(decision);\n    }\n}",
      "c": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\nint normalize(int value) {\n    if (value > 50) {\n        return value - 10;\n    } else {\n        return value + 10;\n    }\n}\n\nint predict(const int history[], int len) {\n    int score = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < len; i++) {\n        score += normalize(history[i]);\n    }\n    return score;\n}\n\nconst char* classify(int score) {\n    if (score >= 150) {\n        return \"THREAT\";\n    } else if (score >= 100) {\n        return \"FLAGGED\";\n    } else {\n        return \"NORMAL\";\n    }\n}\n\nconst char* decide(const char *classification) {\n    if (strcmp(classification, \"THREAT\") == 0) {\n        return \"RESTRICTED\";\n    } else if (strcmp(classification, \"FLAGGED\") == 0) {\n        return \"MONITORED\";\n    }\n    return \"CLEAR\";\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int history[] = {42, 61, 48, 57};\n    int score = predict(history, 4);\n    const char *classification = classify(score);\n    const char *decision = decide(classification);\n\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", score);\n    printf(\"%s\\n\", classification);\n    printf(\"%s\\n\", decision);\n    return 0;\n}",
      "cpp": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n\nint normalize(int value) {\n    if (value > 50) {\n        return value - 10;\n    } else {\n        return value + 10;\n    }\n}\n\nint predict(const std::vector<int>& history) {\n    int score = 0;\n    for (int value : history) {\n        score += normalize(value);\n    }\n    return score;\n}\n\nstd::string classify(int score) {\n    if (score >= 150) {\n        return \"THREAT\";\n    } else if (score >= 100) {\n        return \"FLAGGED\";\n    } else {\n        return \"NORMAL\";\n    }\n}\n\nstd::string decide(const std::string& classification) {\n    if (classification == \"THREAT\") {\n        return \"RESTRICTED\";\n    } else if (classification == \"FLAGGED\") {\n        return \"MONITORED\";\n    }\n    return \"CLEAR\";\n}\n\nint main() {\n    std::vector<int> history = {42, 61, 48, 57};\n    int score = predict(history);\n    std::string classification = classify(score);\n    std::string decision = decide(classification);\n\n    std::cout << score << std::endl;\n    std::cout << classification << std::endl;\n    std::cout << decision << std::endl;\n    return 0;\n}"
    },
