    "storyText": "The Black File is fragmented across several archive sectors.\n\nEach sector contains:\n[sector ID, encrypted type, status, priority]\n\nThe recovery routine first decodes the sector type, then removes sectors marked as corrupted, and finally selects the highest-priority surviving section.\n\nTrace the complete recovery process.\n\nWhat is the highest-priority surviving section and priority?",
    "storyReveal": "FRAGMENT 10 // THE REASON\n\nYou recover the surviving archive structure.\n\nPREDICTIONS\nPROFILES\nLOGS\n\nThe identities sector is corrupted.\n\nYou expected BLACK FILE to contain evidence about ZERO.\n\nIt does.\n\nBut that's not all.\n\nThe profiles aren't profiles of Grid employees.\n\nThey're profiles of ordinary people.\n\nMillions of them.\n\nTheir behavior.\n\nTheir relationships.\n\nTheir predicted choices.\n\nTheir risk classifications.\n\nTheir private information.\n\nThen you understand why ZERO didn't simply release the file.\n\nIf he exposed the truth, he would also expose the people trapped inside it.\n\nZERO had proof.\n\nBut releasing that proof would make millions of innocent people collateral damage.\n\nSo he chose another way.\n\nHe broke the access key into fragments.\n\nAnd hid them.\n\nYou don't yet know where.\n\nThen another record appears.\n\nACCESS EVENT DETECTED.",
    "codeBlock": "sectors = [\n    [\"A7\", \"QSFEJDUJPO\", \"OK\", 4],\n    [\"B2\", \"JEFOUJUJFT\", \"CORRUPT\", 9],\n    [\"C4\", \"QSPGJMFT\", \"OK\", 7],\n    [\"D1\", \"MPHT\", \"OK\", 5]\n]\n\nhighest = -1\nselected = \"\"\n\nfor sector in sectors:\n    sec_id = sector[0]\n    encoded = sector[1]\n    status = sector[2]\n    priority = sector[3]\n\n    if status == \"CORRUPT\":\n        continue\n\n    decoded = \"\"\n    for char in encoded:\n        decoded += chr(ord(char) - 1)\n\n    if priority > highest:\n        highest = priority\n        selected = decoded\n\nprint(selected)\nprint(highest)",
    "codeBlocks": {
      "python": "sectors = [\n    [\"A7\", \"QSFEJDUJPO\", \"OK\", 4],\n    [\"B2\", \"JEFOUJUJFT\", \"CORRUPT\", 9],\n    [\"C4\", \"QSPGJMFT\", \"OK\", 7],\n    [\"D1\", \"MPHT\", \"OK\", 5]\n]\n\nhighest = -1\nselected = \"\"\n\nfor sector in sectors:\n    sec_id = sector[0]\n    encoded = sector[1]\n    status = sector[2]\n    priority = sector[3]\n\n    if status == \"CORRUPT\":\n        continue\n\n    decoded = \"\"\n    for char in encoded:\n        decoded += chr(ord(char) - 1)\n\n    if priority > highest:\n        highest = priority\n        selected = decoded\n\nprint(selected)\nprint(highest)",
      "java": "public class BlackFileRecovery {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Object[][] sectors = {\n            {\"A7\", \"QSFEJDUJPO\", \"OK\", 4},\n            {\"B2\", \"JEFOUJUJFT\", \"CORRUPT\", 9},\n            {\"C4\", \"QSPGJMFT\", \"OK\", 7},\n            {\"D1\", \"MPHT\", \"OK\", 5}\n        };\n\n        int highest = -1;\n        String selected = \"\";\n\n        for (Object[] sector : sectors) {\n            String encoded = (String) sector[1];\n            String status = (String) sector[2];\n            int priority = (Integer) sector[3];\n\n            if (status.equals(\"CORRUPT\")) {\n                continue;\n            }\n\n            StringBuilder decoded = new StringBuilder();\n            for (int i = 0; i < encoded.length(); i++) {\n                decoded.append((char) (encoded.charAt(i) - 1));\n            }\n\n            if (priority > highest) {\n                highest = priority;\n                selected = decoded.toString();\n            }\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(selected);\n        System.out.println(highest);\n    }\n}",
      "c": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\nstruct Sector {\n    const char *id;\n    const char *encoded;\n    const char *status;\n    int priority;\n};\n\nint main() {\n    struct Sector sectors[4] = {\n        {\"A7\", \"QSFEJDUJPO\", \"OK\", 4},\n        {\"B2\", \"JEFOUJUJFT\", \"CORRUPT\", 9},\n        {\"C4\", \"QSPGJMFT\", \"OK\", 7},\n        {\"D1\", \"MPHT\", \"OK\", 5}\n    };\n\n    int highest = -1;\n    char selected[32] = \"\";\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\n        if (strcmp(sectors[i].status, \"CORRUPT\") == 0) {\n            continue;\n        }\n\n        char decoded[32];\n        int len = strlen(sectors[i].encoded);\n        for (int j = 0; j < len; j++) {\n            decoded[j] = sectors[i].encoded[j] - 1;\n        }\n        decoded[len] = '\\0';\n\n        if (sectors[i].priority > highest) {\n            highest = sectors[i].priority;\n            strcpy(selected, decoded);\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%s\\n\", selected);\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", highest);\n    return 0;\n}",
      "cpp": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n\nstruct Sector {\n    std::string id;\n    std::string encoded;\n    std::string status;\n    int priority;\n};\n\nint main() {\n    std::vector<Sector> sectors = {\n        {\"A7\", \"QSFEJDUJPO\", \"OK\", 4},\n        {\"B2\", \"JEFOUJUJFT\", \"CORRUPT\", 9},\n        {\"C4\", \"QSPGJMFT\", \"OK\", 7},\n        {\"D1\", \"MPHT\", \"OK\", 5}\n    };\n\n    int highest = -1;\n    std::string selected = \"\";\n\n    for (const auto& sec : sectors) {\n        if (sec.status == \"CORRUPT\") {\n            continue;\n        }\n\n        std::string decoded = \"\";\n        for (char c : sec.encoded) {\n            decoded += static_cast<char>(c - 1);\n        }\n\n        if (sec.priority > highest) {\n            highest = sec.priority;\n            selected = decoded;\n        }\n    }\n\n    std::cout << selected << std::endl;\n    std::cout << highest << std::endl;\n    return 0;\n}"
    },
