    "storyText": "You trace ADMIN-09's authority.\n\nThe Grid doesn't assign all permissions directly.\nSome accounts inherit privileges from higher-level accounts.\n\nFollow the permission chain.\n\nDetermine the highest authority responsible for the BLACK FILE deletion trail, and the traversal depth reached.",
    "storyReveal": "FRAGMENT 12 // THE OTHER SIDE\n\nYou follow ADMIN-09's authority upward.\n\nADMIN-09\n↓\nSEC-04\n↓\nGRID-OPS\n↓\nGRID-CONTROL\n\nThe deletion trail didn't end with ADMIN-09.\n\nIt led higher.\n\nMuch higher.\n\nULTIMATE AUTHORITY: GRID-CONTROL\n\nYou compare the evidence.\n\nADMIN-09 deleted the records.\n\nBut the authority chain leads somewhere else.\n\nSomeone above him had the power to authorize, restrict, monitor...\n\nand erase.\n\nYou finally understand who wanted ZERO gone.\n\nNot a random administrator.\n\nNot a rogue employee.\n\nThe people who control the Grid.\n\nThen another line appears on your screen.\n\nINVESTIGATION STATUS: COMPROMISED\n\nYOUR ACTIVITY: KNOWN\n\nThey know you're here.\n\nAnd somewhere inside the Grid, ZERO's trail is still waiting.\n\nYou have three fragments left.",
    "codeBlock": "permissions = {\n    \"ADMIN-09\": [\"READ\", \"DELETE\"],\n    \"SEC-04\": [\"AUDIT\"],\n    \"GRID-OPS\": [\"MONITOR\", \"DELETE\"],\n    \"GRID-CONTROL\": [\"AUTHORIZE\", \"RESTRICT\", \"DELETE\"]\n}\n\nparent = {\n    \"ADMIN-09\": \"SEC-04\",\n    \"SEC-04\": \"GRID-OPS\",\n    \"GRID-OPS\": \"GRID-CONTROL\"\n}\n\ncurrent = \"ADMIN-09\"\ndepth = 0\nauthority = \"\"\n\nwhile current in parent:\n    if \"DELETE\" in permissions[current]:\n        authority = current\n    current = parent[current]\n    depth += 1\n\nif \"DELETE\" in permissions[current]:\n    authority = current\n\nprint(authority)\nprint(depth)",
    "codeBlocks": {
      "python": "permissions = {\n    \"ADMIN-09\": [\"READ\", \"DELETE\"],\n    \"SEC-04\": [\"AUDIT\"],\n    \"GRID-OPS\": [\"MONITOR\", \"DELETE\"],\n    \"GRID-CONTROL\": [\"AUTHORIZE\", \"RESTRICT\", \"DELETE\"]\n}\n\nparent = {\n    \"ADMIN-09\": \"SEC-04\",\n    \"SEC-04\": \"GRID-OPS\",\n    \"GRID-OPS\": \"GRID-CONTROL\"\n}\n\ncurrent = \"ADMIN-09\"\ndepth = 0\nauthority = \"\"\n\nwhile current in parent:\n    if \"DELETE\" in permissions[current]:\n        authority = current\n    current = parent[current]\n    depth += 1\n\nif \"DELETE\" in permissions[current]:\n    authority = current\n\nprint(authority)\nprint(depth)",
      "java": "import java.util.*;\n\npublic class PermissionPropagation {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Map<String, List<String>> permissions = new HashMap<>();\n        permissions.put(\"ADMIN-09\", Arrays.asList(\"READ\", \"DELETE\"));\n        permissions.put(\"SEC-04\", Arrays.asList(\"AUDIT\"));\n        permissions.put(\"GRID-OPS\", Arrays.asList(\"MONITOR\", \"DELETE\"));\n        permissions.put(\"GRID-CONTROL\", Arrays.asList(\"AUTHORIZE\", \"RESTRICT\", \"DELETE\"));\n\n        Map<String, String> parent = new HashMap<>();\n        parent.put(\"ADMIN-09\", \"SEC-04\");\n        parent.put(\"SEC-04\", \"GRID-OPS\");\n        parent.put(\"GRID-OPS\", \"GRID-CONTROL\");\n\n        String current = \"ADMIN-09\";\n        int depth = 0;\n        String authority = \"\";\n\n        while (parent.containsKey(current)) {\n            if (permissions.get(current).contains(\"DELETE\")) {\n                authority = current;\n            }\n            current = parent.get(current);\n            depth++;\n        }\n\n        if (permissions.get(current).contains(\"DELETE\")) {\n            authority = current;\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(authority);\n        System.out.println(depth);\n    }\n}",
      "c": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\nstruct AccountPerm {\n    const char *name;\n    const char *perms[4];\n    int perm_count;\n};\n\nstruct ParentLink {\n    const char *child;\n    const char *parent;\n};\n\nint has_delete(const struct AccountPerm accounts[], int count, const char *name) {\n    for (int i = 0; i < count; i++) {\n        if (strcmp(accounts[i].name, name) == 0) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < accounts[i].perm_count; j++) {\n                if (strcmp(accounts[i].perms[j], \"DELETE\") == 0) return 1;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n\nconst char* get_parent(const struct ParentLink links[], int count, const char *child) {\n    for (int i = 0; i < count; i++) {\n        if (strcmp(links[i].child, child) == 0) return links[i].parent;\n    }\n    return NULL;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    struct AccountPerm accounts[4] = {\n        {\"ADMIN-09\", {\"READ\", \"DELETE\"}, 2},\n        {\"SEC-04\", {\"AUDIT\"}, 1},\n        {\"GRID-OPS\", {\"MONITOR\", \"DELETE\"}, 2},\n        {\"GRID-CONTROL\", {\"AUTHORIZE\", \"RESTRICT\", \"DELETE\"}, 3}\n    };\n\n    struct ParentLink links[3] = {\n        {\"ADMIN-09\", \"SEC-04\"},\n        {\"SEC-04\", \"GRID-OPS\"},\n        {\"GRID-OPS\", \"GRID-CONTROL\"}\n    };\n\n    const char *current = \"ADMIN-09\";\n    int depth = 0;\n    char authority[32] = \"\";\n\n    const char *p;\n    while ((p = get_parent(links, 3, current)) != NULL) {\n        if (has_delete(accounts, 4, current)) {\n            strcpy(authority, current);\n        }\n        current = p;\n        depth++;\n    }\n\n    if (has_delete(accounts, 4, current)) {\n        strcpy(authority, current);\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%s\\n\", authority);\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", depth);\n    return 0;\n}",
      "cpp": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <map>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nint main() {\n    std::map<std::string, std::vector<std::string>> permissions = {\n        {\"ADMIN-09\", {\"READ\", \"DELETE\"}},\n        {\"SEC-04\", {\"AUDIT\"}},\n        {\"GRID-OPS\", {\"MONITOR\", \"DELETE\"}},\n        {\"GRID-CONTROL\", {\"AUTHORIZE\", \"RESTRICT\", \"DELETE\"}}\n    };\n\n    std::map<std::string, std::string> parent = {\n        {\"ADMIN-09\", \"SEC-04\"},\n        {\"SEC-04\", \"GRID-OPS\"},\n        {\"GRID-OPS\", \"GRID-CONTROL\"}\n    };\n\n    std::string current = \"ADMIN-09\";\n    int depth = 0;\n    std::string authority = \"\";\n\n    while (parent.find(current) != parent.end()) {\n        const auto& perms = permissions[current];\n        if (std::find(perms.begin(), perms.end(), \"DELETE\") != perms.end()) {\n            authority = current;\n        }\n        current = parent[current];\n        depth++;\n    }\n\n    const auto& final_perms = permissions[current];\n    if (std::find(final_perms.begin(), final_perms.end(), \"DELETE\") != final_perms.end()) {\n        authority = current;\n    }\n\n    std::cout << authority << std::endl;\n    std::cout << depth << std::endl;\n    return 0;\n}"
    },
